{% schema %}
{
  "name": "GSO Product Configurator",
  "target": "section",
  "stylesheet": "gso-product-configurator.css",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "GSO Custom Stock Bag" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Build Your Bag" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "subheading", "label": "Subheading", "default": "Choose your material, finish, bag color, and quantity." },
    { "type": "number", "id": "minimum_quantity", "label": "Legacy minimum quantity (deprecated)", "default": 50 },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout",
      "label": "Layout style",
      "default": "card",
      "options": [
        { "value": "card", "label": "Card" },
        { "value": "compact", "label": "Compact" },
        { "value": "minimal", "label": "Minimal" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "color", "id": "background_color", "label": "Card background", "default": "#120004" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "text_color", "label": "Text color", "default": "#ffffff" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "muted_text_color", "label": "Muted text color", "default": "#d8cfd1" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "accent_color", "label": "Accent color", "default": "#ff1f1f" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "border_color", "label": "Border color", "default": "#ff1f1f" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "field_background", "label": "Dropdown background", "default": "#050505" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "field_text_color", "label": "Dropdown text color", "default": "#ffffff" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "result_background", "label": "Result box background", "default": "#1b080b" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "border_radius", "label": "Border radius", "min": 0, "max": 32, "step": 2, "default": 16 },

    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_price_each", "label": "Show price per unit", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_order_total", "label": "Show order total", "default": false },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_matched_tier", "label": "Show matched tier", "default": false },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_price_breaks", "label": "Show price break chart", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_profit_data", "label": "Show internal profit/cost data", "default": false },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Stock Bag personalization" },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enable_personalization",
      "label": "Enable ADD YOUR BRAND uploads",
      "info": "Stock Bags only. Requires the personalization upload endpoint, the rate-limit migration, and read_files/write_files to be live. Leave OFF until those are deployed.",
      "default": false
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}

{% assign selected_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant %}

{%- comment -%}
  15G.5D: configurator-controlled products get exactly ONE purchase path —
  the GSO configurator. The lockout marker (deterministic, from existing
  product signals: type "Stock Bag" or tag "configurator-pilot") hides the
  theme's native Add to cart / Buy with Shop / More payment options via the
  extension CSS + JS. 16D: canonical launch jars carry the configurator-pilot
  tag, so they lock exactly like bags; the JS also applies the lockout body
  class and blocks native form submits for jars now.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign gso_lockout = false -%}
{%- if product.type == 'Stock Bag' or product.tags contains 'configurator-pilot' -%}
  {%- assign gso_lockout = true -%}
{%- endif -%}

<div
  class="gso-configurator gso-configurator--{{ block.settings.layout }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  {% if gso_lockout %}data-gso-lockout="1"{% endif %}
  data-configurator-proxy="/apps/wholesale-lite/configurator"
  data-checkout-proxy="/apps/wholesale-lite/configurator-checkout"
  data-customer-email="{% if customer %}{{ customer.email | escape }}{% endif %}"
  data-shop="{{ shop.permanent_domain | escape }}"
  data-product-handle="{{ product.handle | escape }}"
  {%- comment -%}
    6A: the canonical product type drives the Zakeke family gate in
    gso-zakeke-bridge.js. Stock Bags never use Zakeke (premade GSO artwork), so
    the bridge must be able to tell families apart without a network call.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  data-product-type="{{ product.type | escape }}"
  data-product-gid="gid://shopify/Product/{{ product.id }}"
  data-base-variant-gid="gid://shopify/ProductVariant/{{ selected_variant.id }}"
  {%- comment -%}
    15G.5C: the saved block-instance setting (64 on the live theme) can never
    retro-update from a schema default change, so customer-facing MOQ no longer
    renders from block settings at all. 50 is the canonical fallback; the
    server's minQuantity overrides everything at runtime.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  data-minimum-quantity="50"
  data-show-price-each="{{ block.settings.show_price_each }}"
  data-show-order-total="{{ block.settings.show_order_total }}"
  data-show-matched-tier="{{ block.settings.show_matched_tier }}"
  data-show-price-breaks="{{ block.settings.show_price_breaks }}"
  data-show-profit-data="{{ block.settings.show_profit_data }}"
  style="
    --gso-card-bg: {{ block.settings.background_color }};
    --gso-text: {{ block.settings.text_color }};
    --gso-muted: {{ block.settings.muted_text_color }};
    --gso-accent: {{ block.settings.accent_color }};
    --gso-border: {{ block.settings.border_color }};
    --gso-field-bg: {{ block.settings.field_background }};
    --gso-field-text: {{ block.settings.field_text_color }};
    --gso-result-bg: {{ block.settings.result_background }};
    --gso-radius: {{ block.settings.border_radius }}px;
  "
>
  <div class="gso-configurator__inner">
    <p class="gso-configurator__eyebrow">{{ block.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
    <h3 class="gso-configurator__title" data-gso-copy="heading">{{ block.settings.heading }}</h3>
    <p class="gso-configurator__subheading" data-gso-copy="subheading">{{ block.settings.subheading }}</p>

    <div class="gso-configurator__loading">Loading custom bag options...</div>

    <div class="gso-configurator__app" hidden>
      <div class="gso-configurator__fields">
        {%- comment -%}
          16D: jar products reuse the same controls with jar vocabulary —
          "material" carries the included Matte/Gloss base finish and
          "finish" carries the universal GSO specialty ladder.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <label class="gso-configurator__field">
          <span>{% if product.type == 'Jars' %}Base Finish (Included){% elsif product.type == 'DTP Pouches' %}Lamination{% elsif product.type == 'Stickers' %}Material{% else %}Material{% endif %}</span>
          <select data-gso-field="material"></select>
        </label>

        <label class="gso-configurator__field">
          <span>{% if product.type == 'Jars' %}Specialty{% elsif product.type == 'DTP Pouches' %}Included Spec{% elsif product.type == 'Stickers' %}Specialty{% else %}Finish{% endif %}</span>
          <select data-gso-field="finish"></select>
        </label>

        <label class="gso-configurator__field">
          <span>Bag Color</span>
          <select data-gso-field="bagColor"></select>
        </label>

        <label class="gso-configurator__field" data-gso-field-row="labelSet" hidden>
          <span>{% if product.type == 'Jars' %}Label Material{% else %}Label Set{% endif %}</span>
          <select data-gso-field="labelSet"></select>
        </label>

        <label class="gso-configurator__field" data-gso-field-row="jarColor" hidden>
          <span>Jar Color</span>
          <select data-gso-field="jarColor"></select>
        </label>

        {%- comment -%}
          16F: dimension inputs for sticker/label products. Hidden by default;
          the JS reveals the row when the server payload sets
          product.dimensionsRequired (dimension-driven pricing families).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <label class="gso-configurator__field" data-gso-field-row="widthIn" hidden>
          <span>Width (inches)</span>
          <input data-gso-field="widthIn" type="number" min="0.5" max="12" step="0.25" value="3">
        </label>

        <label class="gso-configurator__field" data-gso-field-row="heightIn" hidden>
          <span>Height (inches)</span>
          <input data-gso-field="heightIn" type="number" min="0.5" max="12" step="0.25" value="3">
        </label>

        <label class="gso-configurator__field">
          <span>Quantity</span>
          <input data-gso-field="quantity" type="number" min="50" step="1" value="50">
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="gso-configurator__summary">
        <div class="gso-configurator__result" data-gso-result="priceEachBox">
          <span>Price Per Unit</span>
          <strong><span data-gso-result="priceEach">-</span> <small>each</small></strong>
        </div>

        <div class="gso-configurator__result" data-gso-result="orderTotalBox">
          <span>Order Total</span>
          <strong data-gso-result="orderTotal">-</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="gso-configurator__result" data-gso-result="matchedTierBox">
          <span>Matched Tier</span>
          <strong data-gso-result="matchedTier">-</strong>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="gso-configurator__notice" data-gso-result="notice">
        Sides are set to Double Sided. Minimum order is <span data-gso-min-display>50</span> units.
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        17C.1: the Zakeke bridge fills this in once a design is attached, so the
        customer can see their artwork rode along before they add to cart.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="gso-configurator__artwork" data-gso-artwork hidden></div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Phase 3: ADD YOUR BRAND. Two independent gates — the merchant setting
        (default OFF) AND canonical Stock Bag identity. Nothing renders unless
        both hold, so the markup is simply absent for every other family and
        while the feature is off. This is not a CSS-only hide.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign gso_personalization = false -%}
      {%- if block.settings.enable_personalization and product.type == 'Stock Bag' -%}
        {%- assign gso_personalization = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if gso_personalization -%}
        <section
          class="gso-personalization"
          data-gso-personalization
          data-upload-proxy="/apps/wholesale-lite/personalization-upload"
          data-max-files="5"
          data-max-bytes="10485760"
          aria-labelledby="gso-brand-heading-{{ block.id }}"
        >
          <div class="gso-personalization__head">
            <h4 class="gso-personalization__title" id="gso-brand-heading-{{ block.id }}">ADD YOUR BRAND</h4>
            <span class="gso-personalization__optional">OPTIONAL</span>
          </div>
          <p class="gso-personalization__desc">Add your logo and/or QR code to this premade design.</p>

          <label class="gso-personalization__drop" data-gso-personalization-drop for="gso-brand-input-{{ block.id }}">
            <span class="gso-personalization__drop-main">Drop files here or <span class="gso-personalization__browse">browse</span></span>
            <span class="gso-personalization__hint" id="gso-brand-hint-{{ block.id }}">PNG, JPG or PDF &middot; Up to 5 files &middot; 10 MB each</span>
            <input
              id="gso-brand-input-{{ block.id }}"
              class="gso-personalization__input"
              type="file"
              multiple
              accept="image/png,image/jpeg,application/pdf"
              data-gso-personalization-input
              aria-describedby="gso-brand-hint-{{ block.id }}"
            >
          </label>

          <ul class="gso-personalization__list" data-gso-personalization-list></ul>
          <p class="gso-personalization__status" data-gso-personalization-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </section>
      {%- endif -%}

      <button type="button" class="gso-configurator__add" data-gso-add-to-cart>
        Add to Cart
      </button>

      <div class="gso-configurator__breaks" data-gso-result="priceBreaksBox" hidden>
        <div class="gso-configurator__breaks-title">Price Breaks</div>
        <div class="gso-configurator__breaks-table" data-gso-result="priceBreaks"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="gso-configurator__internal" data-gso-result="internalBox" hidden>
        <div>Cost Each: <strong data-gso-result="costEach">-</strong></div>
        <div>Margin: <strong data-gso-result="margin">-</strong></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gso-configurator__error" hidden></div>

    <noscript>
      <div class="gso-configurator__error">Enable JavaScript to use the GSO product configurator.</div>
    </noscript>
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  17C.1: a block may only declare one `javascript` asset in its schema, so the
  Zakeke bridge loads here. It replaces the theme's zakekeBeforeAddToCart (which
  POSTs the $1 canonical variant to /cart/add) with a hand-off into this
  configurator, and blocks native cart writes on configurator products.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  6A: the configurator bundle loads from an explicit deferred script tag rather
  than the block schema's "javascript" key.

  The schema key is Shopify's auto-injection convenience and is capped at 10 KB
  by the AssetSizeAppBlockJavaScript rule; Shopify's own guidance for a larger
  app-block script is to load it from a separate file with a script tag, which is
  exactly how gso-zakeke-bridge.js and gso-personalization.js already load.

  Loading semantics are identical (deferred, once per page, executed before
  DOMContentLoaded fires), so every init path below is unchanged. It is loaded
  FIRST so the two dependent assets always find a fully-parsed configurator.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'gso-product-configurator.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

<script src="{{ 'gso-zakeke-bridge.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{%- comment -%}
  Phase 3: ADD YOUR BRAND client. Self-gating — it exits immediately unless the
  [data-gso-personalization] container is present, which only the merchant
  setting + Stock Bag identity can produce. No network calls while off.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'gso-personalization.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>


